OL,3,GNEWSAOnline racism 'worse now' local
OL,4,Apoliticians say
OL,5,
OL,6,FOnline racist abuse has become more
OL,7,Fconstant and emboldened, a current and
OL,8,Fformer councillor have said.
OL,10,FEhthesham Haque, who represents Barnes
OL,11,Fand Thornhill on Sunderland City
OL,12,FCouncil, said he regularly had to hide
OL,13,Fracist comments on his Facebook posts.
OL,15,F"When I first entered politics, which
OL,16,Fwas about three years ago, it wasn't
OL,17,Fthat bad but now every single post - no
OL,18,Fmatter what it's about - there will be
OL,19,Fa loud minority that will make it about
OL,20,Frace or racism," the Labour councillor
OL,21,Fsaid.
OL,23,APub: 26-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
